\section{Normalizing Crossref metadata}

The raw Crossref shapes are awkward to consume directly---capitalized [[DOI]]
keys, nested date-part arrays, a relation map keyed by relationship name---so we
flatten them into the small, stable dictionaries stored on the [[Paper]] model.
Keeping this translation in one place means the rest of the system never has to
know Crossref's wire format.

\subsection{Formatting notice dates}

Crossref expresses dates as nested \enquote{date-parts} arrays that may be
truncated to just a year, or a year and month, when the full date is unknown.
We render whatever precision is available into an ISO-style string, and treat an
absent or empty date as simply \enquote{no date} rather than failing---the date
is informational, and a missing one must not abort a retraction check.

<<currency normalization helpers>>=
def _format_notice_date(updated: dict | None) -> str | None:
    """Render a Crossref date-parts structure as an ISO-style string."""
    if not updated:
        return None
    parts = updated.get("date-parts") or []
    if not parts or not parts[0]:
        return None
    nums = [n for n in parts[0] if n is not None]
    if not nums:
        return None
    # Year is left as-is; month/day are zero-padded to two digits.
    return "-".join(
        str(n) if i == 0 else f"{n:02d}" for i, n in enumerate(nums)
    )
@

<<test functions>>=
class TestFormatNoticeDate:
    """Tests for _format_notice_date precision handling."""

    def test_full_date(self):
        assert _format_notice_date({"date-parts": [[2010, 2, 6]]}) == "2010-02-06"

    def test_year_only(self):
        assert _format_notice_date({"date-parts": [[2010]]}) == "2010"

    def test_missing_is_none(self):
        assert _format_notice_date(None) is None
        assert _format_notice_date({"date-parts": [[]]}) is None
