\section{The module-level interface}

Callers want three convenient verbs over a single shared client: look up one
DOI, annotate a batch of papers, and reduce a paper to a one-word status.  We
instantiate the client once at import time so its cache and session are shared
across the whole process.

<<module-level currency interface>>=
_client = CrossrefClient()


def fetch_currency(doi: str | None) -> dict | None:
    """Look up currency metadata for a single DOI (see CrossrefClient)."""
    return _client.fetch_currency(doi)
@

\subsection{Annotating a batch of papers}

The batch annotator is what the CLI commands call.  It writes the fetched
currency onto each paper via [[replace]] (the papers are otherwise immutable in
the enrichment style), and---crucially---leaves a paper untouched when the
lookup is undetermined.  That way a paper without a DOI stays unchecked, and a
transient failure never overwrites a currency result a previous run had already
established.

<<module-level currency interface>>=
def annotate_papers(
    papers: list[Paper], progress_callback=None
) -> list[Paper]:
    """Return copies of ``papers`` annotated with Crossref currency data.

    Papers whose DOI cannot be resolved (missing, not found, or a failed
    request) are returned unchanged, preserving any prior currency status.
    ``progress_callback(done, total)`` is invoked after each paper if given.
    """
    annotated = []
    total = len(papers)
    for index, paper in enumerate(papers):
        result = _client.fetch_currency(paper.doi)
        if result is None:
            annotated.append(paper)
        else:
            annotated.append(
                replace(
                    paper,
                    updated_by=result["updated_by"],
                    newer_versions=result["newer_versions"],
                )
            )
        if progress_callback:
            progress_callback(index + 1, total)
    return annotated
@

<<test functions>>=
class TestAnnotatePapers:
    """Tests for annotate_papers."""

    def test_annotates_checked_paper_and_skips_no_doi(self):
        """A DOI paper gets currency; a DOI-less paper is left unchecked."""
        with_doi = Paper(title="A", authors=["x"], doi="10.1/a")
        without_doi = Paper(title="B", authors=["y"])
        with patch.object(
            _client._session, "get", return_value=_mock_response(200, {})
        ):
            out = annotate_papers([with_doi, without_doi])
        assert out[0].updated_by == []  # checked, clean
        assert out[1].updated_by is None  # never checked
